<speak>A straightforward support call, then, with no elaborate preparation. We can keep the invitation wording plain so it is clear what the session is for. It is considerate that you want to avoid turning family help into a standing responsibility. The same principle applies to ordinary scheduling: someone may help you remember an appointment without needing to participate in the conversation itself. We can address invitations directly to you and let you decide how to put them into your own calendar. Do you mostly rely on the calendar on your telephone now, or are you still using a paper diary alongside it?</speak>